{"lines":[{"h":0.014723203769140158,"t":"Test 2","y":0.036219081024978728,"w":0.063786010742187496,"c":1,"x":0.078189299052774566},{"w":0.13608805338541674,"c":1,"x":0.42989836003343174,"h":0.019947764168639415,"t":"READING","y":0.079415652774359247},{"h":0.020359110073992603,"t":"READING PASSAGE 1","x":0.080246915110144534,"c":1,"y":0.13953488336849529,"w":0.31069959004720049},{"y":0.17873969375154763,"h":0.017481236631934904,"t":"You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 1-13, which are based on Reading","w":0.81687240600585942,"c":1,"x":0.08024692462052703},{"t":"Passage 1 below.","w":0.17142819722493488,"h":0.019677283485870944,"y":0.19649585525321578,"x":0.077885782104895662,"c":1},{"y":0.23390357049630217,"h":0.023656400269417288,"c":1,"w":0.37068646748860679,"x":0.3146634821562162,"t":"The White Horse of Uffington"},{"t":"The cutting of huge figures or 'geoglyphs' into the earth of English hillsides has taken","h":0.017474388486504955,"w":0.78600824991861973,"c":1,"y":0.45200235585258453,"x":0.080246903797577901},{"x":0.080181532937399616,"y":0.46919260034344146,"w":0.8231768290201823,"h":0.019649976274290437,"t":"place for more than 3,000 years. There are 56 hill figures scattered around England, with","c":1},{"c":1,"x":0.080177171273774467,"h":0.019975682450688703,"t":"the vast majority on the chalk downlands of the country's southern counties. The figures","y":0.48619676219211705,"w":0.81288818359375004},{"t":"include giants, horses, crosses and regimental badges. Although the majority of these","c":1,"x":0.078107512569949994,"y":0.50407982674799423,"w":0.79648554484049472,"h":0.021190798324746685},{"c":1,"h":0.020482541815552202,"x":0.080150874955377371,"t":"geoglyphs date within the last 300 years or so, there are one or two that are much older.","w":0.81704030354817703,"y":0.52269493997042904},{"h":0.021114596489321125,"w":0.80262532552083343,"c":1,"y":0.54654791302558481,"t":"The most famous of these figures is perhaps also the most mysterious - the Uffington","x":0.080166999717894497},{"y":0.56611367053021244,"c":1,"w":0.7902696736653646,"t":"White Horse in Oxfordshire. The White Horse has recently been re-dated and shown","x":0.082231344376224341,"h":0.018918213771285441},{"c":1,"w":0.80262532552083343,"x":0.080171272045703665,"h":0.018951358727768541,"t":"to be even older than its previously assigned ancient pre-Roman Iron Age* date. More","y":0.5839530478569368},{"t":"controversial is the date of the enigmatic Long Man of Wilmington in Sussex. While many","x":0.082210058344070372,"y":0.60089780543073434,"w":0.83352193196614588,"c":1,"h":0.020540194741688333},{"h":0.017464116549183006,"t":"historians are convinced the figure is prehistoric, others believe that it was the work of an","x":0.080246913524238531,"y":0.62063953472361544,"c":1,"w":0.83333333333333337},{"c":1,"w":0.83139938354492182,"t":"artistic monk from a nearby priory and was created between the 11th and 15th centuries.","y":0.63705076735953636,"x":0.082230006009506362,"h":0.019352628710132325},{"c":1,"w":0.79027684529622388,"t":"The method of cutting these huge figures was simply to remove the overlying grass","x":0.080169471344478896,"y":0.66245142715785588,"h":0.019336983508861483},{"c":1,"x":0.080128850727643058,"t":"to reveal the gleaming white chalk below. However, the grass would soon grow over","y":0.67936823731947615,"h":0.021137193740467297,"w":0.79655303955078116},{"t":"the geoglyph again unless it was regularly cleaned or scoured by a fairly large team","h":0.019415737462127991,"x":0.08017933742507144,"y":0.69837594326221775,"w":0.79233998616536461,"c":1},{"t":"of people. One reason that the vast majority of hill figures have disappeared is that","x":0.082197272647407824,"w":0.78417327880859389,"y":0.71485442012587042,"h":0.020416192368146846,"c":1},{"h":0.017460692757290786,"y":0.73401162774557482,"c":1,"x":0.082304517006095826,"w":0.78600824991861984,"t":"when the traditions associated with the figures faded, people no longer bothered or"},{"y":0.75145348860258177,"w":0.79218104044596349,"c":1,"t":"remembered to clear away the grass to expose the chalk outline. Furthermore, over","h":0.01744185965530165,"x":0.082304546011585933},{"h":0.018491768584234625,"t":"hundreds of years the outlines would sometimes change due to people not always","c":1,"x":0.082246382837760923,"y":0.76967257988869042,"w":0.77790908813476567},{"w":0.74707387288411464,"t":"cutting in exactly the same place, thus creating a different shape to the original","x":0.082225088818486725,"h":0.01946073314185981,"y":0.78688149908694227,"c":1},{"t":"geoglyph. The fact that any ancient hill figures survive at all in England today is","x":0.082231692423662253,"c":1,"y":0.80479075043846848,"w":0.74912068684895838,"h":0.018994069632989552},{"y":0.82055785765946976,"h":0.023731436128470396,"w":0.8274619547526042,"c":1,"t":"testament to the strength and continuity of local customs and beliefs which, in one case","x":0.082165869972491243},{"x":0.084113988699908243,"t":"at least, must stretch back over millennia.","w":0.39547088623046867,"h":0.020688792701604397,"y":0.84049769976609623,"c":1},{"t":"*Iron Age: a period (in Britain 800 BCE - 43 CE) that is characterised by the use of iron tools","h":0.012964685617543492,"x":0.086356729738856136,"y":0.88347225303827059,"w":0.55568796793619801,"c":1},{"x":0.084362139441979192,"t":"38","w":0.026748971939086916,"c":1,"y":0.90843023238112497,"h":0.013081395583944722}],"w":2400,"h":3396}